@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
title Student/professor messaging — implemented send and history flow
actor "Signed-in student\nor professor" as Person
boundary "messaging.js" as UI
control "Messaging API\nLocal demo session" as API
control "createMessagingAccess(db)" as DAL
database PostgreSQL as DB
Person -> UI: Select a peer / conversation
UI -> API: GET conversations/:id/messages
API -> API: Validate HttpOnly session; derive actor ID
API -> DAL: history(actorId, conversationId, cursor?)
DAL -> DB: Verify actor has profile and belongs to conversation
alt Not a participant
  DAL --> API: FORBIDDEN
  API --> UI: 403; no history disclosed
else Participant
  DAL -> DB: Read ordered messages, 50 per page
  DB --> DAL: Messages + older-page flag
  DAL --> API: Conversation peer and history
  API --> UI: Render history and Load older control
end
Person -> UI: Write message and select Send
UI -> UI: Keep draft; generate/reuse clientMessageId
UI -> API: POST conversations/:id/messages\nbody + clientMessageId
API -> API: Verify host, origin, session and JSON limit
API -> DAL: send(session.actorId, conversationId, payload)
DAL -> DB: Verify conversation membership
DAL -> DAL: Validate nonblank text, <= 5000 characters, UUID
alt Unauthorized / invalid
  DAL --> API: FORBIDDEN / validation error
  API --> UI: 403 / 422; preserve draft
else Valid
  DAL -> DB: UPSERT unique(senderId, clientMessageId)\nCreate immutable message if absent
  DB -> DB: Trigger verifies participant sender\nand updates conversation.lastMessageAt on insert
  alt Same ID previously used with different text/conversation
    DAL --> API: CONFLICT
    API --> UI: 409; preserve draft
  else First send or exact retry
    DB --> DAL: One committed message
    DAL --> API: Message
    API --> UI: Render escaped message; clear matching draft
  end
end
note over UI,DB
  Lost acknowledgements retain the draft and retry identifier.
  An exact retry returns the existing row without duplicating it.
  Visible chats poll every 4 seconds; older history is paged.
  Sessions are local development demos, not production authentication.
end note
@enduml
